// rustc borrowck/issue-95079-missing-move-in-nested-closure.rs — upstream captured
// variable cannot escape `FnMut` closure body
// imported batch B167 @ da5114692c9ebe46b869488c5f34f92eb10b98c1 (rust 1.100.0)
// shelf: admit · root bck.NEW-CESC — RE-PORTED AS-IS 2026-09-07 (stage 4)
// ── BUCKET 2: re-ported as-is, still admitted, still a defect. The old port returned
//    the inner closure through a BARE closure type (`fn foo(s:&i64) -> || -> i64`),
//    which is not a Rust type at all; routed through upstream's own boxed/impl-Trait
//    return with its `+ 'a` bound it is STILL admitted, so the shortcut was not the cause.
// ── ROOT RE-CHECKED. The escape channel decides, and only one channel constrains
//    anything — MEASURED PAIR 2026-09-07:
//      Box::new(|| -> i64 { x }) coerced to Box<dyn Fn() -> i64>  -> REFUSED
//      keep(|| -> &i64 { &x }) through a plain generic `keep<F>(f:F)->F` -> ADMITS
//    Here the inner closure IS boxed, but its captured `s` comes from the OUTER
//    closure's environment, and the object-lifetime bound is checked against the
//    enclosing FN's `'a`, not against the outer closure's body — so it passes.
// Original path: tests/ui/borrowck/issue-95079-missing-move-in-nested-closure.rs
// upstream commit: 4b0c9d76ae7d387229caea55cfa73c280b08b8a7
// upstream construct: lines 17-24, `foo3` —
//     pub fn foo3<'a>(bar: &'a X) -> impl Iterator<Item = ()> + 'a {
//         Some(()).iter().flat_map(move |()| {
//             Some(()).iter().map(|()| { bar; }) //~ ERROR captured variable cannot escape
//         })
//     }
// Modifications:
//   · the iterator plane (`Some(()).iter().flat_map(..).map(..)`) -> a plain nested
//     closure pair. Logos has no `Iterator` adaptors; the SUBJECT is the non-`move`
//     INNER closure that borrows the OUTER `move` closure's own capture and then
//     escapes the outer body, and that is kept exactly.
//   · `impl Iterator<Item=()> + 'a` -> `Box<dyn Fn() -> i64 + 'a>` — the `+ 'a` bound,
//     which is what upstream's error is measured against, is kept
//   · `foo1`/`foo2` are separate annotated sites and are not this port
//   · assert -> exit code: `fn main() -> i32`
package issue_95079_missing_move_in_nested_closure;
use logos.mem.boxed;
struct X { a: i64 }
fn foo3<'a>(bar: &'a X) -> Box<dyn Fn() -> i64 + 'a> {
    let outer = move || -> Box<dyn Fn() -> i64 + 'a> {
        let inner = || -> i64 { return bar.a; };
        return Box::new(inner);
    };
    return outer();
}
fn main() -> i32 { return 0i32; }
